WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.000
Today, Web DSH, Web Terminal, and installed managed clients operate in the user's private workspace.

00:09.000 --> 00:19.000
DSH chat does not forward work to another client. A reviewed candidate adds an Agent tasks page.

00:19.000 --> 00:29.000
Web DSH controls the task. Python SDK, Claude Code, or Deep Agents runs behind that control surface.

00:29.000 --> 00:40.000
The SDK uses a private checkpoint. Tasks stream output, support cancellation, and record interrupted recovery.

00:40.000 --> 00:50.000
SDK tool interrupts pause for approval. OpenShell stays disabled until all twenty-five qualification gates pass.

00:50.000 --> 01:00.000
The candidate is not deployed. Build, bounded live acceptance, digest verification, and spoken-content review remain.
